# Force LF line endings for all text files.
# This prevents Windows Git (core.autocrlf=true) from converting shell scripts
# to CRLF, which causes "bash\r: No such file or directory" errors on WSL/Linux.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf

# Binary files — no line ending conversion
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.tar  binary
*.gz   binary

# Keep the desktop client out of the release archive. `app/` is a development tree:
# scripts/install.sh's KEEP_ROOT deletes it on arrival, so every user downloaded 640 KB
# (5.95 MB -> 5.31 MB, 72 entries -> 0) only to have it removed. Measured with
# `git archive HEAD | tar -t | grep -c '^app/'`; note that reading the attribute from an
# UNCOMMITTED .gitattributes needs `git archive --worktree-attributes`, which is why a
# first attempt to verify this concluded, wrongly, that export-ignore does not work.
#
# Deliberately only `app/`. tests/, helpers/, docs/ and packaging/ are also dev-only and
# also stripped client-side, but the install path reads strip-tarball.sh out of the
# extracted archive and packaging/ carries the formula that verify-formula-locally.sh
# builds against — removing those needs a release to prove, and this one does not.
# Verified after adding this line: scripts/cli/devteam and scripts/lib/devteam/*.py
# (the Homebrew formula's whole payload) and all five KEEP_ROOT trees still ship.
app/ export-ignore
